{"open_points":[{"subject":"OwnerFormField identity","kind":"missing identity facts","text":"one field of the owner's pages","question":"Is a field occurrence on each page a distinct OwnerFormField, or do equal names across pages denote one shared field; and, if page membership distinguishes them, must the page or owner action be a fact of the model?","options":["Each page occurrence is distinct and page/action membership is a fact","Equal field definitions across pages are one shared value","Field names are globally unique, so page membership is unnecessary"],"default_guess":"Treat each page occurrence as distinct and add its page or owner action to the facts.","witness":{"initial":"The create-project page and correct-customer page both contain an input named `name` with the same scope and reading kind.","events":["The data provider adds both inputs to the owner form table.","The owner interface renders and reads both pages."],"outcomes":["The two rows are the same value because all declared facts are equal.","The rows are distinct because they belong to different pages."],"observer":"The owner interface implementer sees whether one definition can be changed independently of the other."}},{"subject":"OwnerFormField location","kind":"missing fact","text":"Facts: the field's name; whether it belongs to the request or to its values;
how its text is read.","question":"What fact identifies the precise location that the field reads or fills, including nested members and tuple positions, now that path and tuple-position facts are absent?","options":["OwnerFormField retains a path with tuple positions","The field name alone is the complete location","Another model or page definition supplies the location"],"default_guess":"Retain an explicit path, including tuple positions, as a fact of OwnerFormField.","witness":{"initial":"An owner request contains two nested values whose leaf field is named `id`, one inside the request and one inside a tuple in its values.","events":["The owner submits the form.","The owner interface looks up the OwnerFormField row to construct the request."],"outcomes":["The row carries a path and selects the intended nested or tuple member.","The implementation guesses a location from the name and scope."],"observer":"The product action receiving the request sees different facts populated."}},{"subject":"OwnerFormField destination","kind":"vague fact","text":"whether it belongs to the owner's request itself or to the values the owner gives","question":"What are the closed semantic destinations represented by this fact, and does it say where the parsed value is written or merely classify the field?","options":["A closed two-value destination fact: request or values","A descriptive classification, with a separate destination/path fact","Page-specific destinations beyond request and values are allowed"],"default_guess":"Make it a closed two-value destination fact and combine it with an explicit location."},{"subject":"OwnerFormField closed-list reading","kind":"missing fact","text":"as one of a closed list","question":"For a field read from a closed list, what fact identifies the particular closed list whose member values are accepted?","options":["Each such row references a declared enum or vocabulary","Each row embeds its permitted semantic values","There is one global closed list shared by all such fields"],"default_guess":"Have each row reference a separately declared closed enum or vocabulary.","witness":{"initial":"Two owner fields use different closed lists, such as customer kind and artifact type.","events":["The owner selects a value in each form.","The owner interface reads both submitted texts using their OwnerFormField rows."],"outcomes":["Each row identifies its own closed list and produces a member of the correct domain.","Both rows expose only a generic closed-list reading kind, so the reader must guess which list applies."],"observer":"The owner and the receiving product actions see different accepted values and model facts."}},{"subject":"OwnerFormField row uniqueness","kind":"missing invariant","text":"One row per field.","question":"What makes two rows rows for the same field, and are duplicate names forbidden globally, forbidden only within a page or destination, or permitted when other facts differ?","options":["Names are globally unique and duplicates make the release invalid","Names are unique within a page","The complete tuple of declared facts is the key and duplicate names are allowed"],"default_guess":"Require globally unique names and reject a release containing duplicates.","witness":{"initial":"The provider table contains two rows named `status`, one belonging to the request and one to its values.","events":["A release containing both rows is assembled.","The owner interface looks up `status` while reading a submission."],"outcomes":["The release is invalid because a name must select exactly one row.","Both rows are valid and lookup requires additional facts."],"observer":"The release builder and owner-interface reader see whether the release can be used deterministically."}},{"subject":"OwnerFormField table completeness","kind":"missing read behavior","text":"One row per field.","question":"Is the table a closed, exhaustive set of fields the owner interface may read, and what happens to a submitted or displayed field for which it has no row?","options":["Only named rows are read; an unlisted submitted field is ignored","Every owner form field must have a row; a release missing one is invalid","Unlisted fields are read by a generic fallback"],"default_guess":"Treat the table as exhaustive for readable fields and do not read an unlisted field."},{"subject":"OwnerFormField query fields","kind":"unclear model scope","text":"what the
owner types or picks in a form","question":"Does OwnerFormField also represent owner-page query inputs, or only form-body inputs?","options":["Both form and query inputs are represented","Only form-body inputs are represented","Query inputs use a different model"],"default_guess":"Include both form and query inputs in this model.","witness":{"initial":"An owner list page has a query control for including archived records.","events":["The owner selects the control.","The browser submits it as a query parameter.","The owner interface attempts to read it."],"outcomes":["The query field has an OwnerFormField row and is read through the table.","The model covers only form inputs, so the query field is handled separately or not read."],"observer":"The owner sees whether the requested list selection takes effect."}},{"subject":"OwnerFormField creation authority and source","kind":"vague provenance","text":"The release: the owner form table the data provider holds.","question":"Which named data provider mints or authors OwnerFormField values, from which exact release artifact or constant, and can any other product action create or change them?","options":["The data provider alone authors them in `OWNER_FORM_FIELDS` for each release","The owner interface derives them from its pages","The release assembly derives them from another model or contract"],"default_guess":"The data provider alone supplies them through the release constant `OWNER_FORM_FIELDS`; runtime product actions only read them."},{"subject":"OwnerFormField fields","kind":"standard_violation","text":"Facts: the field's name; whether it belongs to the request or to its values;
how its text is read.","rule":"Указывай все поля с типами","section":"5","question":"Replace the untyped fact list with a complete declaration of every OwnerFormField field and its type."}]}
